From: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ovsdb: do not complete a join with a singleton view

Keep a rejoining server from electing itself before it has observed a
configuration containing the remote members.

Signed-off-by: zhangzujian <zhangzujian.7@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/ovsdb/raft.c b/ovsdb/raft.c
index e50f1f7..546678e 100644
--- a/ovsdb/raft.c
+++ b/ovsdb/raft.c
@@ -4190,7 +4190,13 @@ raft_handle_add_server_reply(struct raft *raft,
     }

     if (rpy->success) {
-        raft_join_complete(raft);
+        /* The add reply can race the configuration log entry.  Do not leave
+         * joining state while the local view still contains only ourselves;
+         * otherwise a transient singleton view can elect this server and
+         * commit entries that the real cluster later overwrites. */
+        if (hmap_count(&raft->servers) > 1) {
+            raft_join_complete(raft);
+        }

         /* It is tempting, at this point, to check that this server is part of
          * the current configuration.  However, this is not necessarily the
--
